1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,000
Welcome to Alexa+, an autonomous multi-service mission execution platform.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Built for the Amazon Developer Hackathon, Alexa+ accepts high-level real-world missions,

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,600
coordinating tools across services to deliver verified, evidence-grounded results.

4
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:20,500
Here is the prototype's primary navigation in the left sidebar.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:27,000
The sidebar provides instant access to every part of the system: the Home launchpad,

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,200
New Conversation, Mission registry, Knowledge Base, MCP Tools, Integrations, Activity, and Settings.

7
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,000
Let's dispatch a real mission. In the composer, we input a high-level goal:

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,200
'Prepare me for my Alexa+ product review tomorrow. Check calendar, find emails, locate documents in Drive,'

9
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:52,300
'identify preparation gaps, and create a checklist.' We select autonomous mode and submit.

10
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:58,000
The prototype executes a five-phase lifecycle: Understand, Plan, Use Tools, Verify, and Result.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The agent interprets temporal constraints, resolves Calendar, Email, and Drive domains,

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,500
and builds a Directed Acyclic Graph plan where each step feeds the next.

13
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:16,500
During execution, the agent connects to our self-hosted MCP server over Streamable HTTP.

14
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:22,000
Watch the tools execute: calendar_get_events retrieves meeting details;

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,500
gmail_search queries discussions matching meeting attendees;

16
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,000
drive_search discovers the architecture document in Drive;

17
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,200
and document_analyze deeply parses the text to extract risks and preparation gaps.

18
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:40,000
Here is the completed mission briefing grounded in retrieved tool evidence.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,500
It confirms schedule, attributes data sources transparently to our local fallback dataset,

20
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:50,600
highlights key architectural decisions, and surfaces critical preparation gaps with an actionable checklist.

21
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:57,000
Navigating to Tools, we inspect our self-hosted MCP server running on port 3001 over Streamable HTTP.

22
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000
All eleven domain tools are dynamically registered using standardized Zod schemas,

23
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,700
with an interactive runner for live testing and latency measurement.

24
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:14,500
On the Integrations page, Alexa+ supports live Google Workspace OAuth with AES-256 encryption.

25
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:20,500
When unauthenticated, the system transparently activates its local SQLite fallback,

26
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:25,100
ensuring reviewers can evaluate every feature with zero configuration.

27
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:31,500
The Activity stream delivers real-time observability via Server-Sent Events, logging state transitions.

28
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:36,500
In Settings, Amazon Bedrock Converse powers agent reasoning

29
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:40,200
using Claude 3.5 Sonnet and Amazon Nova Pro.

30
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:46,500
We also authored mcp-session-reaper, an MIT-licensed package for Streamable HTTP socket hygiene.

31
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:50,500
Alexa+ turns high-level intent into verified action.

32
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,500
Explore the live prototype. Thank you!
